\begin_layout Standard
Define the set of possible y-classes
\begin_inset Formula $\mathcal{C}_{k}\in\{0,1\}$
\end_inset

.
 The optimal deterministic classification strategy is the one that maximizes the probability of succes given 
\begin_inset Formula $x$
\end_inset

:
\begin_inset Formula 
\[
h(x)=\arg\max_{\mathcal{C}_{k}}\mathbb{P}\left(Y=\mathcal{C}_{k}\mid X=x\right)=\begin{cases}
0 & \text{, if }x=0\\
0 & \text{, if }x=1
\end{cases}.
\]

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The risk is calculated where we use the law of total probability and zero-one loss
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
\mathbb{E}\left[\ell\left(y,h(x)\right)\right] & =\sum_{x\in\{0,1\}}\sum_{y\in\{0,1\}}\mathbb{P}\left(Y=y,X=x\right)\ell\left(y,h(x)\right)\\
 & =\sum_{x\in\{0,1\}}\sum_{y\in\{0,1\}}\mathbb{P}(X=x)\mathbb{P}\left(Y=y\mid X=x\right)\ell\left(y,h(x)\right)\\
\\ & =\mathbb{P}(X=0)\mathbb{P}\left(Y=0\mid X=0\right)\ell\left(0,h(0)\right)\\
 & \,+\mathbb{P}(X=0)\mathbb{P}\left(Y=1\mid X=0\right)\ell\left(1,h(0)\right)\\
 & \,+\mathbb{P}(X=1)\mathbb{P}\left(Y=0\mid X=1\right)\ell\left(0,h(1)\right)\\
 & \,+\mathbb{P}(X=1)\mathbb{P}\left(Y=1\mid X=1\right)\ell\left(1,h(1)\right)\\
\\ & =\frac{1}{2}\cdot1\cdot0+\frac{1}{2}\cdot0\cdot1+\frac{1}{2}\cdot0.8\cdot0+\frac{1}{2}\cdot0.2\cdot1\\
 & =\frac{1}{10}.
\end{align*}

