\begin_layout Standard
By direct calculation we get
\begin_inset Formula 
\begin{align*}
\boldsymbol{w}^{\top}\boldsymbol{x}+b & =\ln\left[\frac{\mathbb{P}\left(Y=1\mid X=x\right)}{\mathbb{P}\left(Y=0\mid X=x\right)}\right]\iff\\
-(\boldsymbol{w}^{\top}\boldsymbol{x}+b) & =\ln\left[\frac{\mathbb{P}\left(Y=0\mid X=x\right)}{\mathbb{P}\left(Y=1\mid X=x\right)}\right]\iff\\
\mathbb{P}\left(Y=1\mid X=x\right)\exp\left\{ -(\boldsymbol{w}^{\top}\boldsymbol{x}+b)\right\}  & =\mathbb{P}\left(Y=0\mid X=x\right)=\left(1-\mathbb{P}\left(Y=1\mid X=x\right)\right)\iff\\
1 & =\mathbb{P}\left(Y=1\mid X=x\right)\left(1+\exp\left\{ -(\boldsymbol{w}^{\top}\boldsymbol{x}+b)\right\} \right)\iff\\
\mathbb{P}\left(Y=1\mid X=x\right) & =\frac{1}{1+\exp\left\{ -(\boldsymbol{w}^{\top}\boldsymbol{x}+b)\right\} }=\sigma(\boldsymbol{w}^{\top}\boldsymbol{x}+b).
\end{align*}

\end_inset


\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
That is if 
\begin_inset Formula $\boldsymbol{w}^{\top}\boldsymbol{x}+b$
\end_inset

 encodes the relative probability on log scale of observing 
\begin_inset Formula $Y=1$
\end_inset

 relative to 
\begin_inset Formula $Y=0$
\end_inset

 given 
\begin_inset Formula $X=x$
\end_inset

,
 then the sigmoid function describes the probability of observing 
\begin_inset Formula $Y=1$
\end_inset

.
 
